{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A caller proposes through RawNode or Node.run. Followers may forward; leaders reject proposals during transfer/removal or quota exhaustion. Accepted entries get leader term and consecutive index, enter unstable log and generate deferred self append support. Replication carries preceding index/term, entries and commit. Followers match the preceding entry, refuse committed conflicts, append only the conflicting suffix and acknowledge through the resulting prefix; stale prefixes can acknowledge the existing committed boundary. Ready or asynchronous local append envelopes impose the storage-before-response contract. Successful current-term tracked replies update per-peer Match. The active voter majority order statistic, minimum across both joint halves, supplies a candidate commit index; raftLog advances only when its entry term matches current leader term. Append broadcasts and bounded heartbeat commit propagate the decision. Ready then supplies committed entries, with asynchronous application restricted to locally stable entries and snapshots blocking entry application. Advance or apply response reports completion; the caller owns actual state-machine effects and client acknowledgement. Propose success alone is not commitment.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-entry\",\n        \"B-propose\",\n        \"B-follower-append\",\n        \"B-storage-release\",\n        \"B-aggregate\",\n        \"B-apply\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-app-queued\",\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-apply-reported\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"entry\",\n        \"leader-admit\",\n        \"candidate-follower\",\n        \"send-replication\",\n        \"append-receive\",\n        \"log-start-append\",\n        \"reply-queue\",\n        \"async-contract\",\n        \"leader-match\",\n        \"tracker-commit\",\n        \"majority\",\n        \"joint\",\n        \"log-eligibility\",\n        \"log-apply\",\n        \"ready-contract\",\n        \"node-loop\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Election ticks or Campaign pass eligibility and unapplied-configuration guards. PreVote collects support without changing term/vote; real campaign increments term and records self vote, counted only after deferred response release. Incoming votes require voting eligibility and last term/index freshness. The candidate accepts its phase-specific response type, records first vote per identity and uses active joint voter quorums; winning installs leadership and an empty entry. Higher term normally resets role, votes, remote progress and readOnly acknowledgements, with pre-vote and check-quorum lease exceptions. Lower-term replies do not reach ordinary consumers. Same-term leader traffic demotes candidates. Optional CheckQuorum revokes local leadership on inactive quorum; transfer catches up a voter then sends TimeoutNow, rejects new proposals while pending and aborts on timeout. Application activates membership; learner promotion/removal and joint exit change future quorum interpretation. Restart loads term/vote/commit and membership from Storage then becomes follower. Snapshot restore preserves committed prefix constraints, replaces history/config if needed and prevents campaigning while installation is pending.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-campaign\",\n        \"B-election-result\",\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-vote-queued\",\n        \"F-leader\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-committed\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"campaign\",\n        \"step-vote\",\n        \"roles\",\n        \"term-filter\",\n        \"ticks\",\n        \"candidate-follower\",\n        \"leader-other\",\n        \"tracker-votes\",\n        \"majority\",\n        \"joint\",\n        \"config-change\",\n        \"config-activate\",\n        \"startup\",\n        \"snapshot-restore\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Formation support is scoped by current role/term and interpreted by application-activated membership. Reset discards remote Match and prior vote/read acknowledgements but does not erase log or committed prefix; election freshness and current-term commit gating reconnect inherited history to new decisions. Configuration changes preserve existing peer Match, initialize new peers at zero, and recompute commitment under new voters; staged learners remain outgoing voters until joint exit. Queued storage completions keep their originating raft term: stale entry append completion cannot trim unstable entries, while committed snapshot/application completion remains meaningful across terms. Pending pre-current-term ReadIndex requests survive reset separately from the cleared heartbeat acknowledgement tracker; a subsequent current-term commit reprocesses them through current read mode/quorum. Ready read results still require caller correlation and application progress. Storage, configuration and application boundaries therefore directly govern A1 support and A2 eligibility, without treating mere message emission or applied bookkeeping as durable or client completion.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-storage-release\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-aggregate\",\n        \"B-read\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-read-index\",\n        \"F-apply-reported\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"reset-append\",\n        \"log-eligibility\",\n        \"config-change\",\n        \"config-activate\",\n        \"term-filter\",\n        \"storage-envelope\",\n        \"storage-tail\",\n        \"unstable-stable\",\n        \"apply-progress\",\n        \"read-pending\",\n        \"read-tracking\",\n        \"ready-contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Exact storage failure recovery for a production backend lies beyond the library snapshot; MemoryStorage is not a durable backend.\",\n      \"Detailed read-release liveness under configuration-triggered commitment remains a local question.\",\n      \"Progress flow-control variants and malformed input behavior require separate bounded questions.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core lines have been followed through actual dispatch, producers, quorum consumers, context changes, configuration activation and caller handoffs. Usable is a bounded source explanation, not safety proof or execution evidence.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"66d036cf42454ab7b83ed497e1039f0e\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"66d036cf42454ab7b83ed497e1039f0e\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ad63501da0fe49099ab4a465808db9e9\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"ready_for_check\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"requests\": [],\n        \"question\": \"Can leader commitment of a current-term proposal advance before the replicas whose storage workers have completed matching appends constitute the active voting majority, when the leader append worker is finitely delayed?\",\n        \"importance\": \"Counting an undurable replica toward a required majority can expose committed data to loss after failures. The proposed check observes only the library commitment boundary and storage completion ordering, not crash-induced data loss or client completion.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"append-receive\",\n          \"apply-accept\",\n          \"apply-progress\",\n          \"async-contract\",\n          \"bootstrap\",\n          \"config-activate\",\n          \"durability-expectation\",\n          \"joint\",\n          \"leader-match\",\n          \"log-apply\",\n          \"log-commit-apply\",\n          \"log-eligibility\",\n          \"majority\",\n          \"progress-update\",\n          \"ready-contract\",\n          \"reset-append\",\n          \"startup\",\n          \"step-vote\",\n          \"storage-tail\",\n          \"tracker-commit\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"Leader and non-Byzantine voting followers\",\n          \"Serialized RawNode callers and FIFO local append/apply workers\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"Current-term log entry\",\n          \"Leader committed prefix\",\n          \"Per-voter stored log and Match\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"AsyncStorageWrites with fixed simple voter membership\",\n          \"Leader append worker held while remote append workers and messages run, then released\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"RawNode.Propose -> appendEntry -> deferred self MsgAppResp / remote MsgApp -> follower append -> storage response -> leader Match -> majority -> maybeCommit\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A1\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-aggregate\",\n          \"B-apply\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-committed\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-propose\": \"Produces the current-term target entry and deferred self append response.\",\n          \"B-follower-append\": \"Actual remote producer of append acknowledgements.\",\n          \"B-storage-release\": \"A6 handoff constrains when remote and local acknowledgement support becomes consumable by A1.\",\n          \"B-election-result\": \"Actual election establishes the tested leader, avoiding direct role assignment.\",\n          \"B-membership\": \"Bootstrap and application establish the fixed voter identities used by the oracle.\",\n          \"B-entry\": \"RawNode is serialized and the driver implements asynchronous caller duties.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"establishment\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"send queues self and remote append responses in msgsAfterAppend.\",\n          \"Async Ready envelopes defer these responses until local append completion.\",\n          \"maybeCommit requires a current-term entry and tracker aggregates only active voters.\",\n          \"A follower majority without the leader is legitimate, so local persistence is not an unconditional prerequisite.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether actual self and remote producers, asynchronous Ready collection and commitment consumer preserve the storage-qualified quorum relation in a complete finite execution with held leader writes.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 3,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"The source separates sending replication from publishing support, and initializes self Match during role transitions. A real elected leader and proposal with delayed local appends tests this distinction at the commit endpoint. Two voters make the leader necessary; three voters supply a permitted follower-majority control.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"escalated\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stage\": \"analyze\",\n      \"read_plan_id\": null,\n      \"material_ids\": [],\n      \"spec_task_ids\": [],\n      \"stagnation\": 0,\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Test an explicit persistence-before-counting responsibility without assuming local leader persistence is always necessary.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"current_applicability\": \"within_recorded_scope\",\n      \"executions\": [\n        {\n          \"check_id\": \"1cbbcd58eb824f779c088d377fd008d3\",\n          \"artifact_id\": \"d5859ae3d2754082b6f2257a1ed629d2\",\n          \"action\": \"direct_check\",\n          \"status\": \"completed\",\n          \"outcome\": \"tests_passed\",\n          \"record\": {\n            \"path\": \"state.json\",\n            \"collection\": \"checks\",\n            \"match\": {\n              \"id\": \"1cbbcd58eb824f779c088d377fd008d3\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"ad63501da0fe49099ab4a465808db9e9\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [\n        \"C-storage-qualified-commit\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unit-C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"candidate_id\": \"ad63501da0fe49099ab4a465808db9e9\",\n      \"obligation_ids\": [\n        \"C-storage-qualified-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"D-commit-aggregation\"\n      ],\n      \"relation_ids\": [],\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"description\": \"Storage-qualified leader commitment of ordinary current-term entries in fixed simple configurations under asynchronous Ready processing.\",\n        \"assumptions\": [\n          \"Non-Byzantine messages and honest FIFO storage workers.\",\n          \"No membership changes during the selected proposal interval.\",\n          \"MemoryStorage is the storage-completion model; completed writes are not lost during these executions.\"\n        ],\n        \"excluded\": [\n          \"Physical disk durability and crash recovery\",\n          \"Joint configurations and dynamic membership\",\n          \"Byzantine or forged messages\",\n          \"Global consensus safety or client linearizability conclusions\"\n        ],\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"async_storage_writes\": true,\n          \"configuration\": \"fixed simple voters\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"rationale\": \"Test an explicit persistence-before-counting responsibility without assuming local leader persistence is always necessary.\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"boundary_changes\": [],\n      \"obligation_checks\": {\n        \"C-storage-qualified-commit\": [\n          \"1cbbcd58eb824f779c088d377fd008d3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n        \"C-storage-qualified-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n      \"semantic_readiness\": {},\n      \"coverage_limitations\": [\n        \"Bounded direct comparison completed; local attribution remains pending: Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed\"\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"units\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"unit-C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n          \"version\": 1\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n      \"concern\": \"consensus_safety\",\n      \"description\": \"Under a fixed simple voter configuration and compliant asynchronous storage workers, a leader may count replicas toward commitment of a current-term entry only after matching log entries have completed storage writes on those replicas; an advanced committed prefix must therefore be backed by a voting majority of such replicas.\",\n      \"scope\": {\n        \"description\": \"Storage-qualified leader commitment of ordinary current-term entries in fixed simple configurations under asynchronous Ready processing.\",\n        \"assumptions\": [\n          \"Non-Byzantine messages and honest FIFO storage workers.\",\n          \"No membership changes during the selected proposal interval.\",\n          \"MemoryStorage is the storage-completion model; completed writes are not lost during these executions.\"\n        ],\n        \"excluded\": [\n          \"Physical disk durability and crash recovery\",\n          \"Joint configurations and dynamic membership\",\n          \"Byzantine or forged messages\",\n          \"Global consensus safety or client linearizability conclusions\"\n        ],\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"async_storage_writes\": true,\n          \"configuration\": \"fixed simple voters\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"durability-expectation\",\n        \"async-contract\",\n        \"majority\",\n        \"log-eligibility\"\n      ],\n      \"pending\": [],\n      \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n      \"candidate\": true,\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"reply-queue\",\n          \"reset-append\",\n          \"leader-match\",\n          \"tracker-commit\",\n          \"majority\",\n          \"log-eligibility\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"durability-expectation\",\n          \"async-contract\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"D-commit-aggregation\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"The implementation explicitly requires entries to be persisted before being counted toward commitment (durability-expectation). The async contract permits outgoing replication before local writes but requires storage-worker responses after ordered durable completion. Under a fixed simple voting configuration, commitment may use any majority of persisted matching replicas; it does not require the leader itself to have persisted when other replicas form a majority. This requirement is independent of the observed committed value and of a blanket expectation that delayed local writes block every commit.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Non-Byzantine peers; stable fixed simple voter membership; async storage mode; current-term ordinary proposal; honest ordered storage workers, no crashes or data corruption. MemoryStorage represents successfully completed storage writes at the library boundary; no physical disk durability is measured.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"A three-voter leader may legally commit using both followers while its own append worker is delayed.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"claims\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n          \"version\": 1\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d5859ae3d2754082b6f2257a1ed629d2\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"plan_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run/direct-checks/7cee079f6c8641afbcbecb7c4d1af5fa/plan.json\",\n      \"harness_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run/direct-checks/7cee079f6c8641afbcbecb7c4d1af5fa/assurance_generated_test.go\",\n      \"unit_id\": \"unit-C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"graph_versions\": {\n        \"C-storage-qualified-commit\": 1,\n        \"D-commit-aggregation\": 1,\n        \"unit-C-storage-qualified-commit\": 1\n      },\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"direct_checks\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"d5859ae3d2754082b6f2257a1ed629d2\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"claims\",\n          \"match\": {\n            \"id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n            \"version\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"bindings\",\n          \"match\": {\n            \"id\": \"D-commit-aggregation\",\n            \"version\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"units\",\n          \"match\": {\n            \"id\": \"unit-C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n            \"version\": 1\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assessments\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"direct_check_id\": \"d585