ring the applicable requirement, selected entry and caller duties, oracle, identity, legal history, observation completion and contrary evidence. Applicability and decomposition are separate questions, not mandatory extra essays: include them when a concrete issue needs that answer. Seek weaker/stronger contracts, alternative mechanisms and unmet dependencies. For models, inspect behavior and checker separately, including trigger reachability and excluded branches. No issue found is provisional, neither a proof nor an independent vote.\n\nCURRENT VERSION Cite unchanged established parts and focus on the increment: what changed, which premise it answers, what the new execution observed and what remains unanswered. New driver inputs require their own actual execution and correspondence; old review success cannot certify them. Scope/cause/consequence questions outside the checked proposition are independent limits, not additional confirmation gates. Never alter a requirement or weaken a predicate merely to obtain a passing test.\n\nISSUES Fixed Claim, Harness and Monitor conflicts have exact issue/condition records. Address the listed issue with a sourced resolution and, where supplied, condition dispositions; do not answer the same conflict separately in several products. A no_issue_found item alone clears nothing. Preserve current counterevidence as an open issue, explained alternatives in rationale and independent limits in limitations. Resolution applies to its answering version and descendants; it does not legalize an older driver. Shared semantic issues follow actual dependencies, not checker names.\n\nREPAIR Distinguish review aspect from challenged component. Driver/configuration/initialization changes preserve the requirement and oracle, replace only sourced current premises, and need fresh execution. Changed observation/oracle encoding uses explicit correction; changed normative meaning/applicability uses F2, and proposition-preserving dependency expansion us